  summary: "A legal and economic proposition stating that where there are complete competitive markets with no transaction costs, an efficient set of inputs and outputs to and from production-optimal distribution will be selected, regardless of how property rights are divided. It suggests that private parties can solve externalities through bargaining. It is a cornerstone of environmental and property law policy.",
