  summary: "Consequentialism is an ethical framework asserting that the morality of an action is determined solely by its outcomes. Utilitarianism, championed by Jeremy Bentham and John Stuart Mill, is the most prominent form, arguing that the best action is the one that maximizes overall happiness or utility. It provides a pragmatic approach to decision-making by focusing on the net benefit to society.",
