  label: "Critical labor studies and workplace surveillance theory (Zuboff, Ball)",
  summary: "This field examines how digital monitoring and algorithmic management transform the power dynamics between employers and employees. It highlights the erosion of worker autonomy, the intensification of labor, and the psychological impact of constant observation. These theories are essential for policymakers addressing the future of work and digital labor rights.",
