  summary: "World-systems theory analyzes the global economy as a single unit divided into core, semi-periphery, and periphery regions, characterized by unequal exchange. It emphasizes the historical development of capitalism as a global system that shapes the political and economic possibilities of individual nations. It is a standard lens for analyzing global inequality and international development.",
