  summary: "Critiques of GDP argue that Gross Domestic Product is an insufficient metric for national well-being because it ignores environmental degradation, income inequality, and non-market activities like care work. These critiques advocate for alternative indicators that capture a more holistic view of social and economic health. This movement is central to debates about sustainable development and inclusive growth.",
