  summary: "A theory describing a process by which a product or service takes root initially in simple applications at the bottom of a market and then relentlessly moves upmarket, eventually displacing established competitors. It explains how new technologies can fundamentally change industry structures. Policymakers use this to understand the impact of emerging technologies on legacy industries.",
  example: "",
  frequency: "Category: economic_theory",
