  summary: "Financial regulation history examines the evolution of laws and oversight mechanisms designed to maintain market integrity and protect investors. The formation of the SEC, for example, was a direct response to the market failures of the Great Depression, establishing a framework for transparency and accountability. Understanding this history helps policymakers anticipate the consequences of deregulation and market innovation.",
