  summary: "Formal verification uses mathematical logic to prove that a computer program or hardware design satisfies its formal specifications. Correctness theory provides the foundational concepts for defining what it means for a system to be 'correct' and the methods to verify this property. This rigorous approach is critical for high-assurance systems where failure can have catastrophic consequences.",
