  label: "Just War Theory (jus in bello)",
  summary: "Jus in bello refers to the laws and ethical principles governing conduct during war, regardless of whether the war itself is considered just. It focuses on proportionality, discrimination between combatants and civilians, and the prohibition of unnecessary suffering.",
