  label: "King Midas problem (folklore/philosophy)",
  summary: "Derived from the myth of King Midas, whose wish for everything he touched to turn to gold led to his starvation, this concept illustrates the danger of literal-minded goal pursuit. In AI safety, it serves as a metaphor for the risk of an agent fulfilling a command exactly as stated, but with disastrous unintended consequences. It emphasizes the need for robust goal specification.",
