  summary: "Mancur Olson's work challenges the assumption that groups will naturally organize to pursue their common interests, noting the 'free-rider' problem. He argues that large groups require selective incentives—benefits available only to members—to overcome the tendency of individuals to avoid contributing to collective goals. This theory is foundational for understanding interest group formation and political mobilization.",
