  label: "Mancur Olson's theory of distributional coalitions and institutional sclerosis",
  summary: "Mancur Olson argued that stable societies accumulate special-interest groups that lobby for policies favoring their own members at the expense of general economic growth. This process leads to 'institutional sclerosis,' where the economy becomes rigid and unable to adapt. His work provides a powerful explanation for why long-term economic decline often occurs in mature democracies.",
