  summary: "These models involve the continuous, systematic collection, analysis, and interpretation of health-related data to plan, implement, and evaluate public health practices. They are essential for detecting disease outbreaks and monitoring the health status of populations to inform policy interventions. By providing real-time insights, these frameworks enable governments to allocate resources effectively during health crises.",
