  label: "Safety engineering traditions emphasizing fault tree analysis and FMEA",
  summary: "These are systematic methodologies used to identify potential failure modes and their causes within complex systems. Fault Tree Analysis uses a top-down deductive approach to identify root causes, while Failure Mode and Effects Analysis (FMEA) evaluates the severity and likelihood of individual component failures. These techniques are foundational for ensuring reliability in high-stakes industries like aerospace and nuclear power.",
