  summary: "An economic theory centered on the concept of 'creative destruction,' where innovation by entrepreneurs leads to the obsolescence of old industries and the birth of new ones. It highlights the role of technological change as the primary driver of long-term economic growth. This perspective is vital for understanding industrial policy and the impact of disruptive technologies.",
