  summary: "Thermodynamics is the branch of physics that deals with heat, work, and temperature, and their relation to energy and physical properties of matter. Its laws govern the limits of efficiency and the direction of energy flow in all physical systems. These principles are increasingly applied to understand the energy consumption of computing and industrial processes.",
