  summary: "Human factors engineering applies psychological and physiological principles to the design of products, processes, and systems. Endsley’s model specifically focuses on situation awareness, defining it as the perception of elements in the environment, the comprehension of their meaning, and the projection of their status in the near future. This framework is critical for policy decisions regarding high-stakes environments like aviation, healthcare, and nuclear power.",
